{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7115050","formula":"C₁₄H₁₈F₃NO","hill":"C14H18F3NO","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"F":3.0,"H":18.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Oxaflozane"},"descriptions":{"en":"Oxaflozane (INN; brand name Conflictan) is an antidepressant and anxiolytic drug that was introduced by Solvay in France in 1982 for the treatment of depression but has since been discontinued. It is a prodrug of flumexadol (N-dealkyloxaflozane; 2-(3-trifluoromethylphenyl)morpholine; CERM-1841 or 1841-CERM), which is reported to act as an agonist of the serotonin 5-HT1A (pKi = 7.1) and 5-HT2C (pKi = 7.5) receptors and, to a much lesser extent, of the 5-HT2A (pKi = 6.0) receptor. In addition to its serotonergic properties, oxaflozane may also produce anticholinergic side effects at high doses, namely in overdose."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":432824,"mass":273.29,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)N1CCOC(C1)C2=CC(=CC=C2)C(F)(F)F","inchikey":"FVYUQFQCEOZYHZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-propan-2-yl-2-[3-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]morpholine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"432824","atoms":37,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.769,"y":-1.083,"z":-0.055,"el":"F"},{"x":-3.041,"y":-2.39,"z":-0.151,"el":"F"},{"x":-3.482,"y":-1.308,"z":1.683,"el":"F"},{"x":1.14,"y":1.172,"z":1.528,"el":"O"},{"x":3.156,"y":-0.056,"z":-0.067,"el":"N"},{"x":1.737,"y":-0.115,"z":-0.451,"el":"C"},{"x":0.998,"y":1.114,"z":0.102,"el":"C"},{"x":3.88,"y":-1.218,"z":-0.58,"el":"C"},{"x":3.277,"y":0.029,"z":1.394,"el":"C"},{"x":2.515,"y":1.248,"z":1.906,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.476,"y":1.073,"z":-0.241,"el":"C"},{"x":5.357,"y":-1.128,"z":-0.206,"el":"C"},{"x":3.702,"y":-1.3,"z":-2.093,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.262,"y":0.002,"z":0.185,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.049,"y":2.107,"z":-0.981,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.62,"y":-0